on. That is not the same as a grant, and no grant should be inferred from it.

Two things are outside this notice, and deliberately so.

1. THE GAME. Go belongs to nobody. Its rules, its proverbs, the classical
   life-and-death problems, and the game records of the old masters are the
   common inheritance of everybody who sits down at a board. Nothing in this
   notice claims any of them. Where this project has set them in its own
   words (the translations, the lessons, the commentary), those words are the
   Studio's, and the position underneath them is nobody's.

2. OTHER PEOPLE'S SOFTWARE AND TYPE. This project is built on open-source
   software and on typefaces drawn by other people, each under its own terms.
   Those terms govern those components, not this notice. The full list is in
   `src/content/legal.js`, shown to every reader on the Credits page in the
   app, and the type is documented file by file in `src/fonts/LICENSES.md`.

Asking is welcome. A request to use a piece of this for teaching, for a club,
or for a go server that is not trying to be this one has never yet been turned
down: hello@northboundsoftwarestudio.com.
